./analysis/cross_agent_screening_agreement_current_3ds_2gpt/cross_model_decisions.csv:14:benchmark:9,Generative pretraining from large-scale transcriptomes: Implications for single-cell deciphering and clinical translation,"Exponential accumulation of single-cell transcriptomes poses great challenge for efficient assimilation. Here, we present an approach entitled tGPT towards integration of 22.3 million single-cell transcriptomes by modeling gene expression rankings as generative pretraining task. tGPT is conceptually simple in that it autoregressively models the ranking of a gene in the context of its preceding neighbors. We demonstrated the high performance of tGPT on a range of fundamental single-cell analysis tasks and novel applications on bulk tissues. The single-cell clusters and cell lineage trajectories derived from tGPT are highly aligned with known cell labels and states. The feature patterns of tumor bulk tissues learned by tGPT are associated with a wide range of genomic alteration events, prognosis and treatment outcome of immunotherapy. tGPT represents a new analytical paradigm for integrating and deciphering massive amount of transcriptome data and it will facilitate the interpretation and clinical translation of single-cell transcriptomes.",benchmark_boundary_case,Generative pretraining from large-scale transcriptomes: Implications for single-cell deciphering and clinical translation,"Exponential accumulation of single-cell transcriptomes poses great challenge for efficient assimilation. Here, we present an approach entitled tGPT towards integration of 22.3 million single-cell transcriptomes by modeling gene expression rankings as generative pretraining task. tGPT is conceptually simple in that it autoregressively models the ranking of a gene in the context of its preceding neighbors. We demonstrated the high performance of tGPT on a range of fundamental single-cell analysis tasks and novel applications on bulk tissues. The single-cell clusters and cell lineage trajectories derived from tGPT are highly aligned with known cell labels and states. The feature patterns of tumor bulk tissues learned by tGPT are associated with a wide range of genomic alteration events, prognosis and treatment outcome of immunotherapy. tGPT represents a new analytical paradigm for integrating and deciphering massive amount of transcriptome data and it will facilitate the interpretation and clinical translation of single-cell transcriptomes.",benchmark_boundary_case,EXCLUDE,EC2_no_text_component,,primary_model_paper,no,no,yes,yes,,,,,"tGPT models gene expression rankings autoregressively without any natural-language text, prompt, caption, or explicit text-bio alignment, so it does not meet the text component criterion. | The abstract presents tGPT, an autoregressive generative model pretrained on 22.3 million transcriptomes, demonstrating broad applicability across single-cell and bulk tissue tasks, which qualifies as a generative text-bio foundational model.","tGPT models gene expression rankings autoregressively without any natural-language text, prompt, caption, or explicit text-bio alignment, so it does not meet the text component criterion.","The abstract presents tGPT, an autoregressive generative model pretrained on 22.3 million transcriptomes, demonstrating broad applicability across single-cell and bulk tissue tasks, which qualifies as a generative text-bio foundational model.",,Generative pretraining from large-scale transcriptomes: Implications for single-cell deciphering and clinical translation,"Exponential accumulation of single-cell transcriptomes poses great challenge for efficient assimilation. Here, we present an approach entitled tGPT towards integration of 22.3 million single-cell transcriptomes by modeling gene expression rankings as generative pretraining task. tGPT is conceptually simple in that it autoregressively models the ranking of a gene in the context of its preceding neighbors. We demonstrated the high performance of tGPT on a range of fundamental single-cell analysis tasks and novel applications on bulk tissues. The single-cell clusters and cell lineage trajectories derived from tGPT are highly aligned with known cell labels and states. The feature patterns of tumor bulk tissues learned by tGPT are associated with a wide range of genomic alteration events, prognosis and treatment outcome of immunotherapy. tGPT represents a new analytical paradigm for integrating and deciphering massive amount of transcriptome data and it will facilitate the interpretation and clinical translation of single-cell transcriptomes.",benchmark_boundary_case,EXCLUDE,EC2_no_text_component,,primary_model_paper,no,no,yes,yes,,,,,"tGPT models gene expression rankings autoregressively; no natural language text or text-bio alignment present; excludes as text component missing. | The paper presents tGPT, an autoregressive model trained on gene expression rankings from 22.3 million single-cell transcriptomes with generative pretraining, but it operates on biological tokens (gene rankings) rather than natural language text.",tGPT models gene expression rankings autoregressively; no natural language text or text-bio alignment present; excludes as text component missing.,"The paper presents tGPT, an autoregressive model trained on gene expression rankings from 22.3 million single-cell transcriptomes with generative pretraining, but it operates on biological tokens (gene rankings) rather than natural language text.",,Generative pretraining from large-scale transcriptomes: Implications for single-cell deciphering and clinical translation,"Exponential accumulation of single-cell transcriptomes poses great challenge for efficient assimilation. Here, we present an approach entitled tGPT towards integration of 22.3 million single-cell transcriptomes by modeling gene expression rankings as generative pretraining task. tGPT is conceptually simple in that it autoregressively models the ranking of a gene i