./analysis/cross_agent_screening_agreement/unstable_reasoning_cases.csv:3:1198,Big Bird: Transformers for Longer Sequences,exclude_uncertain_unstable,UNCERTAIN|EXCLUDE|EXCLUDE|EXCLUDE,UNCERTAIN,EC2_no_substantive_text_bio_bridge,bio_modality_unclear,,,,,"The abstract presents BigBird as a general NLP transformer improvement with a mention of genomics applications but no central biological modality or text-bio bridge; bio modality is unclear from the abstract. | The abstract describes an encoder-only sparse attention transformer (BigBird) for longer sequences, referencing BERT and tasks like question answering and summarization, but does not mention any generative mechanism such as decoder, autoregressive, or diffusion. Therefore it is not a generative model.",EXCLUDE,EC1_no_bio_modality,,clear_exclude,NLP tasks such as question answering and summarization,none,none,Abstract presents a transformer architecture for NLP without biological modality or explicit generative mechanism. Excluded under EC1_no_bio_modality.,EXCLUDE,EC2_no_substantive_text_bio_bridge,,clear_include,improves performance on various NLP tasks such as question answering and summarization,none,none,"BigBird introduces a new transformer architecture (primary model) with NLP tasks (text component) and mentions genomics applications (bio modality), but provides no explicit text‑bio integration or generative decoder, so it is included as a primary model without a text‑bio bridge or generative component.",EXCLUDE,EC2_no_substantive_text_bio_bridge,,,,,,"The abstract presents BigBird as a new transformer model with NLP improvements (text component) and mentions novel applications to genomics data (bio modality), but provides no explicit description of a text‑bio mapping or bridge. | BigBird is presented as a sparse-attention transformer improving long‑context NLP tasks; the abstract contains no mention of decoder, autoregressive or other generative mechanisms. It highlights broad applicability to many NLP