./analysis/cross_agent_screening_agreement/unstable_reasoning_cases.csv:37:1961,Rethinking Genomic Modeling Through Optical Character Recognition,stable_include,UNCERTAIN|EXCLUDE|INCLUDE|EXCLUDE,UNCERTAIN,,text_component_unclear,thin_abstract_boundary,OCR-capable vision-language model with document decoder and prompt-conditioned objectives,vision-language model processing DNA visual layouts,masked span completion and prompt-conditioned objectives,"Abstract presents OpticalDNA as a vision-language model for genomic modeling with masked span completion, but does not clearly describe natural-language text input or text-bio alignment, leaving text component and bridge uncertain.",EXCLUDE,EC2_no_text_component,,clear_exclude,none,none,masked span completion,"OpticalDNA uses a vision-language model on visual DNA layouts but does not describe natural-language text input or output; text component absent, leading to exclusion under EC2_no_text_component.",INCLUDE,,,,,,,"The abstract presents OpticalDNA as a new vision‑language model for DNA that uses prompt‑conditioned objectives and a document decoder, indicating a substantive text component and a central text‑bio bridge. | The abstract presents OpticalDNA with a visual encoder and a document decoder that performs masked span completion, indicating a generative decoder, and reports broad pretraining and strong performance across diverse genomic benchmarks, showing foundation‑model traits.",EXCLUDE,EC3_not_generative,,,,,,"The paper introduces OpticalDNA, a vision‑language model that encodes DNA visually and decodes text via a document decoder and prompt‑conditioned objectives, establishing a clear bio‑text bridge. | The abstract presents a vision‑language model with encoder/decoder for compression and masked span completion, but provides no explicit generative mechanism such as autoregressive DNA generation.",thin_or_truncated_abstract;text_component_boundary;generative_boundary
