unaligned biological sequences to multiple sequence alignments. The abstract mentions NLP techniques, but no substantive text/language modality in the candidate model itself.","evidence_snippet":"\"trains transformers to map a set of unaligned biological sequences to an MSA\""},{"record_id":"rec_000320","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The model operates on DNA promoter sequences with BERT-style pre-training and a dictionary-based segmentation scheme. That is bio-sequence modeling, not a clearly substantive text-bio generative model.","evidence_snippet":"\"a novel DNA sequence segmentation method\"; \"utilizes it for BERT pre-training\""}]}
