review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly states this is a narrative review of AI applications in cardio-oncology. It summarizes prior work rather than presenting a new candidate model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This narrative review summarizes contemporary artificial intelligence applications in cardio-oncology\"."},{"record_id":"rec_003485","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Primary multimodal neuro-MRI model with multi-omics validation in Crohn's disease. The abstract does not describe any text/language component.","evidence_snippet":"\"a multimodal neuro-MRI model\" and \"Multi-omics\" were used to decode mechanisms and predict progression."},{"record_id":"rec_003486","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Primary multimodal AI framework aligning histopathology and spatial transcriptomics. The candidate model is image-plus-omics, not text-bio.","evidence_snippet":"\"bridge this gap, we develop a multimodal AI framework\" transferring spatial molecular information from ST into histopathology-derived representations."},{"record_id":"rec_003487","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_substantive_text_bio_bridge","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a primary ncRNA modeling paper and it explicitly uses a language model, but the abstract describes only biological sequence modeling, not a text-bio bridge. The text-like component is not a substantive text modality.","evidence_snippet":"\"integrates the nucleic-acid language model GENA-LM\" and \"all-token representation strategy\"."},{"record_id":"rec_003488","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Primary cross-modal analysis linking mutation-selection profiles to histopathology. It uses bio data and image features, but no text/language component is described.","evidence_snippet":"\"cross-modal analysis\" between \"somatic mutations\" and \"H&E-stained whole slide images\"."}]}
